c Dysfunction + with severly impaired LV relaxation, Increased LAP.\r\n\r\nMild to Mod MR +\r\nMyxomatous AML.\r\n\r\nMod TR + TVMax 38mmhg.\r\nPAP 48mmhg\r\nConcentric LVH +\r\n\r\nNo LA /LV thrombus seen.\r\n\r\nIntact IAS, IVS, no abnormal pressure gradient noted across IAS or IVS.\r\n\r\nPulmonary Artery Pressure raised. PAP 48mmhg.\r\n\r\nMild Pericardial Effusion seen.\r\n\r\nIVC normal size and good collapse with respiration.\r\n\r\nPericardium Normal.\r\n\r\nNo abnormal mid LV cavity turbulence or SAM.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAdvised: Regular Follow Up. Diet and Life Style Changes, regular check up’s.\r\n\r\n\r\nPS: The echocardiographic findings are amenable to change with disease progression or improvement and with medication.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDr. Sample Admin\r\nMBBS, MD Medicine\r\nFormer Professor & HOD Medicine, ANIIMS.\r\nFellow Clinical Cardiology Fellow 2D Echocardiography',0,NULL,'2025-01-12 18:30:00','2026-05-03 20:42:06'),
