(14,'Inferior MI with RV Involvement','ihd','Inferior MI extending to RV — dilated RV with reduced TAPSE.','{\"rv_wall_thickness\":\"5\",\"rv_dimension\":\"38\",\"tapse\":\"13\",\"ivc_size\":\"24\",\"ivs\":\"10\",\"lvpw\":\"10\",\"lv_edd\":\"50\",\"lv_esd\":\"38\",\"epss\":\"8\",\"mapse\":\"11\",\"la_size\":\"40\",\"ao_root\":\"32\",\"ef_percent\":\"48%\",\"fs_percent\":\"24%\",\"lap_ee\":\"11\",\"pap\":\"30\",\"lv_diastolic_function\":\"Grade I - Impaired Relaxation\",\"lv_systolic_function\":\"Mildly reduced (EF 45-54%)\",\"ea_ratio\":\"E\\/A &lt;1.0 - Grade I\",\"ivs_motion\":\"Paradoxical Motion\",\"pericardium_status\":\"Normal\",\"rv_longitudinal_function\":\"Severely reduced\",\"rv_transverse_function\":\"Moderately reduced\",\"rv_paradoxical_movement\":\"Present\",\"ias_status\":\"Intact\",\"pericardial_effusion\":\"Trivial\",\"mv_velocity\":\"90\",\"mv_gradient\":\"2\",\"mitral_valve\":\"Mild MR\",\"av_velocity\":\"150\",\"av_gradient\":\"8\",\"aortic_valve\":\"Normal - no AS, no AR\",\"tv_velocity\":\"270\",\"tv_gradient\":\"4\",\"tricuspid_valve\":\"Moderate TR\",\"pv_velocity\":\"110\",\"pv_gradient\":\"10\",\"pulmonary_valve\":\"Mild PR\",\"impression\":\"Inferior wall myocardial infarction with RV involvement.\\n\\n1. Normal LV size with regional akinesia of inferior and infero-septal walls.\\n2. Mildly reduced LV systolic function. EF = 48%.\\n3. Moderately dilated RV (RVID 38 mm).\\n4. Severely reduced RV systolic function (TAPSE 13 mm).\\n5. Paradoxical septal motion.\\n6. Dilated IVC (24 mm) with reduced respiratory collapse \\u2014 elevated RA pressure.\\n7. Moderate TR. Mild pulmonary hypertension.\\n8. No pericardial effusion.\\n\\nCONCLUSION: Inferior MI with significant RV involvement and RV dysfunction.\",\"recommendations\":\"Pre-load dependent \\u2014 AVOID nitrates and diuretics in the acute phase.\\nIV fluid loading guided by clinical response.\\nDAPT, statin, beta-blocker (cautious).\\nUrgent coronary angiography \\/ revascularization.\\nMonitor for AV block (RCA territory).\",\"anterior_motion\":\"Normal\",\"anteroseptal_motion\":\"Normal\",\"inferior_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"inferoseptal_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"lateral_motion\":\"Normal\",\"posterior_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"apex_motion\":\"Normal\",\"rwma_comments\":\"RV free-wall hypokinesia consistent with RV infarction. Paradoxical septal motion. Dilated IVC.\"}',1,NULL,'2026-05-25 08:52:02','2026-05-25 08:52:02'),
(15,'Extensive Anterior + Inferior MI (severe LV dysfunction)','ihd','Multi-territory MI — extensive WMA, severely reduced EF, eccentric remodeling.','{\"rv_wall_thickness\":\"5\",\"rv_dimension\":\"26\",\"tapse\":\"15\",\"ivc_size\":\"22\",\"ivs\":\"8\",\"lvpw\":\"8\",\"lv_edd\":\"66\",\"lv_esd\":\"56\",\"epss\":\"14\",\"mapse\":\"7\",\"la_size\":\"46\",\"ao_root\":\"32\",\"ef_percent\":\"25%\",\"fs_percent\":\"15%\",\"lap_ee\":\"18\",\"pap\":\"44\",\"lv_diastolic_function\":\"Grade III - Restrictive\",\"lv_systolic_function\":\"Severely reduced (EF &lt;35%)\",\"ea_ratio\":\"E\\/A &gt;2.0 - Grade III Restrictive\",\"ivs_motion\":\"Normal \\/ Intact\",\"pericardium_status\":\"Normal\",\"rv_longitudinal_function\":\"Mildly reduced\",\"rv_transverse_function\":\"Mildly reduced\",\"rv_paradoxical_movement\":\"Absent\",\"ias_status\":\"Intact\",\"pericardial_effusion\":\"Trivial\",\"mv_velocity\":\"110\",\"mv_gradient\":\"3\",\"mitral_valve\":\"Moderate MR\",\"av_velocity\":\"130\",\"av_gradient\":\"7\",\"aortic_valve\":\"Normal - no AS, no AR\",\"tv_velocity\":\"310\",\"tv_gradient\":\"5\",\"tricuspid_valve\":\"Moderate TR\",\"pv_velocity\":\"110\",\"pv_gradient\":\"12\",\"pulmonary_valve\":\"Moderate PR\",\"impression\":\"Extensive multi-territory myocardial infarction (anterior + inferior).\\n\\n1. Moderately dilated LV (LVIDD 66 mm) with eccentric remodeling.\\n2. Akinesia of anterior wall, anterior septum, apex, inferior and infero-septal walls.\\n3. Severely reduced LV systolic function. EF = 25%.\\n4. Grade III (restrictive) diastolic dysfunction.\\n5. Moderately dilated LA (46 mm).\\n6. Moderate functional MR (tethering), moderate TR.\\n7. Moderate pulmonary hypertension (PAP 44 mmHg).\\n8. No LV thrombus seen, no pericardial effusion.\\n\\nCONCLUSION: Multi-territory ischemic cardiomyopathy with severely reduced EF and moderate functional MR.\",\"recommendations\":\"URGENT cardiology referral.\\nGDMT: beta-blocker, ACEi\\/ARBi\\/ARNi, MRA, SGLT2i.\\nDiuretics for volume overload. Salt and fluid restriction.\\nViability study before any revascularization decision.\\nICD primary prevention + CRT assessment if QRS wide.\\nConsider advanced HF therapies (LVAD, transplant) if refractory.\",\"anterior_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"anteroseptal_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"inferior_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"inferoseptal_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"lateral_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"posterior_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"apex_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"rwma_comments\":\"Extensive multi-territory wall motion abnormalities. Tethered mitral leaflets \\u2014 moderate functional MR. No discrete aneurysm, no thrombus seen at time of study.\"}',1,NULL,'2026-05-25 08:52:02','2026-05-25 08:52:02'),
(16,'Ischemic Cardiomyopathy (multivessel CAD, global hypokinesia)','ihd','Multivessel CAD producing global hypokinesia — distinguished from DCM by ischemic etiology.','{\"rv_wall_thickness\":\"5\",\"rv_dimension\":\"26\",\"tapse\":\"16\",\"ivc_size\":\"22\",\"ivs\":\"9\",\"lvpw\":\"9\",\"lv_edd\":\"62\",\"lv_esd\":\"52\",\"epss\":\"12\",\"mapse\":\"8\",\"la_size\":\"44\",\"ao_root\":\"32\",\"ef_percent\":\"30%\",\"fs_percent\":\"16%\",\"lap_ee\":\"16\",\"pap\":\"38\",\"lv_diastolic_function\":\"Grade III - Restrictive\",\"lv_systolic_function\":\"Severely reduced (EF &lt;35%)\",\"ea_ratio\":\"E\\/A &gt;2.0 - Grade III Restrictive\",\"ivs_motion\":\"Normal \\/ Intact\",\"pericardium_status\":\"Normal\",\"rv_longitudinal_function\":\"Mildly reduced\",\"rv_transverse_function\":\"Mildly reduced\",\"rv_paradoxical_movement\":\"Absent\",\"ias_status\":\"Intact\",\"pericardial_effusion\":\"Trivial\",\"mv_velocity\":\"110\",\"mv_gradient\":\"3\",\"mitral_valve\":\"Moderate MR\",\"av_velocity\":\"130\",\"av_gradient\":\"7\",\"aortic_valve\":\"Normal - no AS, no AR\",\"tv_velocity\":\"290\",\"tv_gradient\":\"4\",\"tricuspid_valve\":\"Moderate TR\",\"pv_velocity\":\"110\",\"pv_gradient\":\"10\",\"pulmonary_valve\":\"Mild PR\",\"impression\":\"Ischemic cardiomyopathy.\\n\\n1. Dilated LV (LVIDD 62 mm).\\n2. Global LV hypokinesia, worse in territories of prior infarction.\\n3. Severely reduced LV systolic function. EF = 30%.\\n4. Grade III (restrictive) diastolic dysfunction. Elevated LV filling pressure (E\\/e\' 16).\\n5. Moderately dilated LA (44 mm).\\n6. Moderate functional (tethering) MR, moderate TR.\\n7. Moderate pulmonary hypertension (PAP 38 mmHg).\\n8. No LV thrombus. No pericardial effusion.\\n\\nCONCLUSION: Ischemic cardiomyopathy with severely reduced EF, restrictive filling and secondary functional MR.\",\"recommendations\":\"GDMT: beta-blocker, ACEi\\/ARBi\\/ARNi, MRA, SGLT2i.\\nDiuretics for volume overload.\\nCoronary angiography + viability assessment for revascularization.\\nICD primary prevention. CRT if QRS >150 ms and LBBB.\\nConsider Mitraclip \\/ TEER for severe functional MR if EF persistently low.\\nCardiac rehab and salt\\/fluid restriction.\",\"anterior_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"anteroseptal_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"inferior_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"inferoseptal_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"lateral_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"posterior_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"apex_motion\":\"Hypokinetic\",\"rwma_comments\":\"Global LV hypokinesia, worse in territories of prior infarction. Tethered mitral leaflets \\u2192 moderate functional MR.\"}',1,NULL,'2026-05-25 08:52:02','2026-05-25 08:52:02'),
(17,'Old Anterior MI with Concentric LVH (HTN + CAD)','ihd','Hypertensive heart + old anterior MI — septal thinning vs LVH overlap.','{\"rv_wall_thickness\":\"4\",\"rv_dimension\":\"22\",\"tapse\":\"18\",\"ivc_size\":\"20\",\"ivs\":\"8\",\"lvpw\":\"14\",\"lv_edd\":\"54\",\"lv_esd\":\"42\",\"epss\":\"9\",\"mapse\":\"10\",\"la_size\":\"44\",\"ao_root\":\"34\",\"ef_percent\":\"40%\",\"fs_percent\":\"22%\",\"lap_ee\":\"14\",\"pap\":\"32\",\"lv_diastolic_function\":\"Grade II - Pseudonormal\",\"lv_systolic_function\":\"Moderately reduced (EF 35-44%)\",\"ea_ratio\":\"E\\/A 1.0-2.0 - Grade II Pseudonormal\",\"ivs_motion\":\"Hypertrophied\",\"pericardium_status\":\"Normal\",\"rv_longitudinal_function\":\"Normal\",\"rv_transverse_function\":\"Normal\",\"rv_paradoxical_movement\":\"Absent\",\"ias_status\":\"Intact\",\"pericardial_effusion\":\"None\",\"mv_velocity\":\"100\",\"mv_gradient\":\"3\",\"mitral_valve\":\"Moderate MR\",\"av_velocity\":\"150\",\"av_gradient\":\"8\",\"aortic_valve\":\"Normal - no AS, no AR\",\"tv_velocity\":\"250\",\"tv_gradient\":\"4\",\"tricuspid_valve\":\"Mild TR\",\"pv_velocity\":\"110\",\"pv_gradient\":\"10\",\"pulmonary_valve\":\"Normal - no PR\",\"impression\":\"Hypertensive heart disease with superimposed old anterior MI.\\n\\n1. Mildly dilated LV (LVIDD 54 mm).\\n2. Asymmetric wall thickness: thinned anterior septum (IVS 8 mm \\u2014 regional scar) and concentric thickening of posterior and lateral walls (LVPW 14 mm \\u2014 hypertensive LVH).\\n3. Akinetic mid-distal anterior wall, anterior septum and apex (old MI).\\n4. Moderately reduced LV systolic function. EF = 40%.\\n5. Grade II diastolic dysfunction (pseudonormal).\\n6. Mildly dilated LA (44 mm).\\n7. Moderate functional MR, mild TR.\\n8. Mild pulmonary hypertension (PAP 32 mmHg).\\n\\nCONCLUSION: Old anterior MI on a background of hypertensive heart disease. Moderately reduced LV systolic function and Grade II diastolic dysfunction.\",\"recommendations\":\"Strict BP control (target <130\\/80) \\u2014 ACEi\\/ARB preferred.\\nGDMT: beta-blocker, MRA, SGLT2i.\\nHigh-intensity statin + antiplatelet.\\nAddress lipid, glycemic and renal status.\\nCoronary angiography \\/ viability assessment if not done.\\nRepeat echo in 6 months. ICD assessment if EF persistently <35%.\",\"anterior_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"anteroseptal_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"inferior_motion\":\"Normal\",\"inferoseptal_motion\":\"Normal\",\"lateral_motion\":\"Normal\",\"posterior_motion\":\"Normal\",\"apex_motion\":\"Akinetic\",\"rwma_comments\":\"Thinned anterior wall and apex (old infarct) against a background of concentric thickening of posterior \\/ lateral walls (hypertensive LVH).\"}',1,NULL,'2026-05-25 08:52:02','2026-05-25 08:52:02');
