(2302,'ENC/2026/00031',576,1,186,NULL,'2026-05-06','00:05:12','New Visit','Open',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Burning epigastric pain, sour eructations, occasional nausea x few days.</p><p><br></p><p>AF anticoagulation review. CHA₂DS₂-VASc &amp; HAS-BLED reassessment.</p>','<p>Epigastric burning, retrosternal discomfort, worse on empty stomach / lying down. No haematemesis, no melaena, no weight loss.</p><p><br></p><p>Known AF — paroxysmal / persistent. No new bleeding, no chest pain, no syncope, no neurological deficit. Compliance with anticoagulation reviewed.</p>','<p><br></p>','<p><br></p>','<p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'<p>Soft abdomen, mild epigastric tenderness. No guarding, no rigidity. Bowel sounds normal.</p><p><br></p><p>HR irregularly irregular / sinus today. BP documented. No bruising, no melaena. CVS – variable S1 intensity / no murmur. CHA₂DS₂-VASc = __ , HAS-BLED = __ .</p>','<p>Acute gastritis / GERD.</p><p><br></p><p>Atrial Fibrillation — rate / rhythm controlled, on appropriate anticoagulation.</p>','<p>PPI before food x 2 weeks. Avoid spicy/oily food, late meals, alcohol, smoking. Small frequent meals, head-end elevation. Endoscopy if symptoms persist &gt; 4 weeks or alarm features.</p><p><br></p><p>Continue DOAC + rate control as below. Patient education on missed-dose protocol &amp; bleeding red flags. Avoid NSAIDs. Repeat ECG / Holter as needed.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-05-05 18:35:12','2026-05-05 19:22:54'),
(2303,'ENC/2026/00032',199,1,187,NULL,'2026-05-06','01:14:41','New Visit','Open',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Acute lower back pain after lifting / awkward movement.</p>','<p>Pain onset, character, radiation. Red flags – fever, weight loss, night pain, bowel/bladder, saddle anaesthesia, weakness, trauma – all denied.</p>','<p><br></p>','<p><br></p>','<p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'<p>Mild paraspinal spasm, restricted lumbar flexion. SLR negative bilaterally. Neuro – power, sensations, reflexes intact. No saddle anaesthesia.</p>','<p>Mechanical / muscular acute low back pain — no red flags.</p>','<p>Stay active — avoid bed rest. Hot fomentation, NSAIDs short course, muscle relaxant. Posture correction, core strengthening once acute pain settles. Reassure good prognosis (&gt;90% recover within 6 weeks). Imaging ONLY if red flags.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-05-05 19:44:41','2026-05-05 19:45:03'),
(2304,'ENC/2026/00033',198,1,188,NULL,'2026-05-06','01:17:12','New Visit','Open',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'120','80',72.0,98.6,99.0,16.0,'100','<p>CKD review with stable creatinine. BP, fluid, anaemia, mineral-bone disorder reassessment.</p>','<p>c</p><p><br></p><p>Known CKD. No haematuria, frothy urine, or new oedema. Reviews salt/protein restriction &amp; medication compliance. Asks about appetite, nausea, fatigue, leg cramps.</p>','<p><br></p>','<p><br></p>','<p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'<p>Mild paraspinal spasm, restricted lumbar flexion. SLR negative bilaterally. Neuro – power, sensations, reflexes intact. No saddle anaesthesia.</p><p><br></p><p>BP / weight / pedal oedema documented. Pallor / no pallor. CVS / RS – clear. Recent labs – Hb, eGFR, K+, Ca, PO4, PTH, Vit D documented.</p>','<p>Mechanical / muscular acute low back pain — no red flags.</p><p><br></p><p>CKD Stage 3a / 3b / 4 (eGFR __ ml/min) — etiology DM / HTN.</p>','<p>BP target &lt;130/80. ACEi or ARB if proteinuria. SGLT2i renoprotective. Statin. Salt &lt;5g/day. Avoid nephrotoxins (NSAIDs, contrast, gentamicin). Iron / EPO if Hb low. Phosphate binders &amp; active vit D as below. Refer dialysis planning if eGFR &lt; 20.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-05-05 19:47:12','2026-05-05 21:27:49'),
